  V1 THE PRE-REGISTERED FAMILY TABLE: the 5 SM masses x n = {0,1,2} = 15 members (m_i/100.531^n) vs the 3-rung ladder at the 1% tolerance.  15 x 3 = 45 comparisons, expected count <N> = 0.10 (the null's window math: only m_e/100.531 = 5.0830 keV sits within +-10% of the 5.09-keV rung; L1 (334 K = 2.878e-5 keV) and L2 (9.17 K = 7.906e-7 keV) have ZERO members within +-10%, the family's smallest member m_e/100.531^2 = 0.0506 keV being 1756x above L1).  One survivor: m_e/100.531 vs L0 at 0.11% -- the A01 hook itself.  No other member comes within 1% of ANY rung (next closest: m_mu/100.531^2 = 10.45 keV at 2.05x L0; everything else >= 18x).

  V2 THE SURVIVORS: exactly ONE member survives at the 1% tolerance -- m_e/100.531 = 5.083 keV vs the committed m band rung 5.0886 keV, delta -0.11%, z = -0.058 sigma vs G212 (inside the 1-sigma band [4.992, 5.186]).  This is the PRE-EXISTING A01 hook that DEFINED the family -- its survival is by construction, not evidence.  ADDITIONAL survivors at other SM scales: 0.  The same 3-Z^2-class structure appears at NO other SM mass scale.

  V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT -- THE NUMBER THAT TELLS: the 3-Z^2 sequence is CLOSED.  Pre-registered expectation <N> = 0.10 coincidences in the 15-member family at the 1% tolerance; the run finds the expected single member (m_e/100.531 = 5.083 keV vs the 5.09-keV ladder, the A01 hook) and ZERO additional members: m_mu/100.531-class (1050.8, 10.45 keV), m_p/100.531-class (9333, 92.84 keV), m_n/100.531-class (9346, 92.97 keV), m_tau/100.531-class (17675, 175.8 keV), m_e/100.531^2 (50.6 eV) all miss every ladder rung by >= 100% (most by >= 10x).  The gate is closed twice over: (i) FDR - the hook's own chance rate is E_chance = 0.10 = 300x ABOVE the family-wise E* = 3.3e-4 (THRESHOLD.py), and pre-registered as impassable for the family (any survivor carries its own +-10% presence); (ii) MECHANISM - the only framework reading on record (100 = 3 Z^2 - 0.53%) is the m_e hook itself and generalizes to NO other scale, so no next member exists to carry it.  FINAL REGISTER: m_e/100 is a SINGLE COINCIDENCE (the A01 hook at z = +0.22 sigma against G212, with the 3-Z^2 hook at 0.53% post-hoc); the sequence test CLOSES the question - the mechanistic hook has no next member.

